00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.600
Kiriakou.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.600
Kiriakou, a beautiful Greek name

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.600
from a man from Rhodes.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.600
That's where he's from.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.600
John's an author, radio host,

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.600
and most gnarly, a whistle-blower

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.600
who exposed illegal CIA

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.600
torture program

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.600
and served prison time for it.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.600
Thanks, John, for being here, my brother.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.600
Okay, let's talk a bit about

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.600
your foundational life.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.600
You're from both parents of Greek?

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.600
Yeah, both parents are Greek,

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.600
born in the United States,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.600
but of Greek parents.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.600
Where'd you grow up?

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.600
I grew up in western Pennsylvania,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.600
just north of Pittsburgh,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.600
up in Amish Country.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.600
Ah, I know that very well.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.600
Is that sure that's Amish?

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.600
Amish was near Downingtown,

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.600
Coatesville area.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.600
They spread all across

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.600
Pennsylvania and into Ohio.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.600
Wow, I always thought

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.600
that out west there,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.600
they weren't there.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.600
That was the steel towns.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.600
Yeah.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.600
Yeah, rust buckets,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.600
steel towns now.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.600
Okay, so when all of a sudden

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.600
you grew up in PA,

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.600
did you go to college?

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.600
Yeah, I went to college

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.600
at George Washington University.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.600
I got a bachelor's degree

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.600
in Middle Eastern studies there,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.600
and then I stayed for a master's degree

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.600
in policy analysis.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.600
And then, as it turned out,

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.600
one of my advisors was not really

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.600
a professor there.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.600
He was actually a CIA officer

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.600
undercover as a professor there.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.600
And he recruited me into the CIA.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.600
Wow, and then,

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.600
what year was this we're talking about?

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.600
That was 1988.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.600
Wow, that was,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.600
you look too young to be around there.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.600
Thank you.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.600
I feel like a tired old man.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.600
Did you know I asked me

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.600
to be in the CIA too?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.600
No, I did not know that.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.600
I knew this guy.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.600
All of a sudden, I told him,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.600
this was before 9-11.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.600
And I told him, you know,

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.600
I'd like to help my country.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.600
I'd like to go into the CIA.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:40.600
So he says, really,

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.600
Bo, I said, yeah.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.600
So he says, somebody will contact you.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.600
What was that?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.600
I get a phone call,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.600
and they tell me to meet

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.600
under the old clock

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.600
in Peacock alley

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.600
at the Waldorf Astoria.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.600
Someone will contact you.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.600
Yes.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.600
So all of a sudden,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.600
I'm standing there

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.600
at 12 noon,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.600
and then all of a sudden I hear,

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.600
Boudito.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:03:59.600
I'm looking around.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.600
It was a woman,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.600
about four foot tall.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.600
Hey, Boudito.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.600
And she flashes this

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.600
double-sided identification,

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.600
CIA.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.600
And I said,

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.600
how you doing?

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.600
She goes, my name is so-and-so.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.600
I said, oh.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.600
And then she sits to me now

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.600
and she goes, you know,

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.600
we looked, you're over.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.600
You had a great career

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.600
as a New York City

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.600
homicide detective.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.600
Why do you want to be in the CIA?

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.600
I said, I love my country.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.600
I just feel as though

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.600
I'm not doing enough.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.600
I'm a private investigator.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:24.600
I travel around the world.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.600
That could be my cover.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.600
I could go to Abadabadu

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.600
wherever I got to go.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.600
And I could make

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.600
believe I'm investigating

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.600
something else

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.600
when I'm investigating

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.600
the Abadabadu.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.600
So all of a sudden,

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:36.600
she's there.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.600
She's listening to me.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.600
So she says, OK,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.600
somebody else will contact you.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.600
And I'll never forget,

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.600
she gave me a card

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.600
and it's called

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.600
Something Fox Farms

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.600
in Virginia.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.600
Fox.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.600
Remember, it was like,

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.600
oh, you know what they do

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.600
with the fox?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
They blow the horn.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.600
Yeah.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.600
And that in signal

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.600
was on as something

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.600
Fox Farms.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.600
And that must have been

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.600
a CIA location there.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.600
So everything was good.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.600
The next day,

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.600
I used to do

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.600
Imus in the morning.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.600
Remember, Imus,

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.600
the radio guy?

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.600
Yeah, 34 years,

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.600
I did him.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:05.600
And yeah,

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.600
until he retired.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:07.600
So I mean,

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.600
I'm a little bit

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.600
keeping secrets.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.600
That's what I tell you.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.600
So the next day,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.600
I hit,

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.600
I hit the Imus.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.600
He had ways and

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:15.600
he's dead.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.600
I'm getting,

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.600
because I'm really,

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:18.600
I can't believe that

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:19.600
they're reaching out to me

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.600
to be a CIA operative.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.600
So I said,

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.600
I can't tell you, Don.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.600
He's a wattball.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.600
I said,

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.600
you want me to really tell you,

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.600
I've been contacted

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:28.600
by the CIA

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.600
to be an operative

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.600
in the Middle East.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.600
You know,

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.600
I know all these Saudi

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.600
Arabian guys.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.600
I spent a lot of time

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.600
there.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.600
Put it this way.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.600
After I blasted it out

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.600
on the Imus

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.600
in the morning,

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.600
they never freaking call me.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.600
They said,

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.600
this guy can't keep a secret

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.600
for one day.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.600
That was my CIA operative

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.600
responsibility there.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.600
Let's talk about you.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.600
I never became a CIA operative.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.600
Sorry.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.600
I can't keep the secret.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.600
All right.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.600
So then you were,

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.600
this is in the 1980s.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.600
Okay.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.600
So you went over

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.600
to Middle East after that.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.600
I started off as an analyst.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:01.600
I spent the first seven

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:02.600
and a half years

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:03.600
of my career there

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.600
as an analyst

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:05.600
working on Iraq.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.600
A lot of that was

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.600
overseas, mostly in the

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.600
version.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.600
Was there a need to

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.600
listeners working on Iraq?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:11.600
What does that mean?

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.600
Well, you know,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.600
the CIA does

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.600
many things.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.600
One is analysis

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.600
and the other is operations.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.600
In analysis,

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.600
usually,

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.600
you sit in a cubicle

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.600
in headquarters,

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.600
you think the big thoughts,

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.600
you write papers

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.600
that nobody's ever going to

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:24.600
read,

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.600
and then you send them

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.600
over to the White House.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.600
And every couple of years

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.600
you go overseas,

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.600
maybe you stay

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:30.600
for a year, two,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.600
three years,

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:32.600
you become an expert,

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.600
you learn to speak

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.600
the language,

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.600
and then you come back

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:36.600
and transfer.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:37.600
Were you fluent

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.600
in Arabic?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.600
I was fluent in Arabic.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.600
I have a,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.600
I have a knack

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.600
for foreign languages

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:43.600
and they recognized

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:44.600
that early on,

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.600
so they took advantage

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.600
of it.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.600
What's that dialect

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.600
that all the terrorists

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:51.600
use?

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.600
What's that dialect?

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.600
Fusha.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.600
Footcock?

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:55.600
Fusha.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.600
Oh, Fusha.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.600
Okay, good.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.600
Fusha.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.600
And then I learned

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.600
Khalidjig,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.600
Gulf dialect as well,

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.600
because I spent so much

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.600
time in Saudi Arabia,

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.600
Kuwait, Bahrain.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.600
I was in Saudi Arabia

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.600
in the late,

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.600
the late 70s

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:11.600
and the early 80s,

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.600
I used to go to Riyadh,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.600
and we'd fly to,

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.600
what's that place

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.600
called in the Red Sea?

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.600
Jeddah.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.600
Jeddah.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:19.600
And then there was supposed

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.600
to be no alcohol

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.600
in Saudi Arabia.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.600
And the palace

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.600
that I was in,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.600
they had more booze

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:25.600
than the bar downstairs.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.600
And then we used

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.600
to fly to Jeddah,

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.600
and we would bang

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.600
the Middle Eastern

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:30.600
airline students

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.600
with all the princes.

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.600
We'd give them

